{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485560,"name":"idan lin","username":"idan_lin","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/i/ec9cab/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T16:20:26.481Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485560-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485560-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485560-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485560-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn a \u003cstrong\u003epersonal Cursor Ultra\u003c/strong\u003e account (not Cursor Teams), asking a Bot to create a \u003cstrong\u003ePublic\u003c/strong\u003e shareable template fails every time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe export tool / account guidance says this account can \u003cstrong\u003eonly create PUBLIC\u003c/strong\u003e templates (do not ask about TEAM). We pass \u003ccode\u003evisibility: \"public\"\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe server still returns:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eError: [failed_precondition] A team must be selected to share a team template.\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo review/publish card appears, so no \u003ccode\u003ehttps://x.ai/bot/\u0026lt;id\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e link is created and nobody can \u003cstrong\u003eAdd to Grok Bot\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePersonal Ultra dashboard has no “Public template sharing” toggle (that control is documented for Teams/Enterprise admins). In-app Send Feedback was also submitted earlier for the same issue. Related public note: \u003ca href=\"https://x.com/eddiearc6/status/2096654499838673322\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eIdan Lin on X: \"Tried to publish a Public Grok Bot template on personal Cursor Ultra. Tooling says this account can only create Public templates. Server returns: \"A team must be selected to share a team template.\" No review card, no https://t.co/cZBvFeehoK link — so nobody can Add it. Share as te… / X\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis looks like Public export is incorrectly routed through the \u003cstrong\u003eteam-template\u003c/strong\u003e path.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485560-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485560-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign in with personal Cursor Ultra (no Team).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen any Bot → ask it to create / share a Public template (\u003ccode\u003ecreate_bot_share_json\u003c/code\u003e with \u003ccode\u003evisibility: \"public\"\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve the failed_precondition error above; no review card / no x.ai/bot link.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485560-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485560-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePublic template export succeeds (or clearly fails with a documented personal-account limitation). If Public is supported for Ultra, a review card and \u003ccode\u003ex.ai/bot\u003c/code\u003e link should appear. If not supported, hide Share-as-template / do not document Public-only for this account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485560-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485560-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485560-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485560-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\